pocket-motion-only: glyphs drawn as outlines are PATH ops (0042, 71), which only this rasteriser draws, and colour glyphs are PATH ops under PAINT_PUSH (0019); no upstream backend is taught either, so a stream carrying them stops there.

0063 — text the FONT ATLAS cannot hold, and colour glyphs. The atlas stores
its cell height, baseline, line height, advances and kern deltas in bytes, so
a size whose cell passes 255 px was refused (0002: 176 px for Noto Sans SC,
217 px for HarmonyOS Sans), and its cells stay upright under a rotation.
A codepoint no face mapped was laid out and drawn as the tofu box, and the
only trace of it was a counter nothing read.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`: the
  FONT VECTOR blob ('DCFV'): a slot's glyphs as outlines (PATH TABLE verbs,
  f32 px, origin on the baseline at the pen), each glyph a list of layers
  painted in the run's text colour, a colour of its own, or a gradient (kind,
  six coefficients over the glyph's px, 2 to 6 stops — PAINT_PUSH's own
  terms), with the atlas's metrics in u16/i16 fields. Flag bit 2 marks a
  SUPPLEMENT: an atlas slot's colour glyphs, keyed `ui:font.<slot>.v`.
- `engine/core/src/text.rs`: `VectorFace::parse` (refuses truncation,
  trailing bytes, an unsorted cmap or kern section, an index out of range, a
  verb stream that does not consume its points, a non-finite point, a
  gradient PAINT_PUSH could not draw); `Fonts::load` tells the two blobs by
  magic, a vector face owning its slot's metrics and an atlas replacing it;
  `measure_run_provider` and `layout_run` read metrics from whichever owns
  the slot. A miss keeps its codepoint (`missed_codepoints`, at most 64).
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: a vector slot's run is laid out as the atlas's
  is and each glyph's layers filled as PATH ops through the node's world
  affine — so the glyph turns and scales with its node — the anchor rounded
  to a pixel exactly where GLYPH_RUN rounds it (an axis-aligned world of
  scale 1); a text stroke outlined from the same outlines (outside: twice
  the width, under the fill; centred: over it). An atlas slot's colour
  glyphs are left out of GLYPH_RUN and the glyph pages and drawn as layers
  after them. A gradient layer is PAINT_PUSH (its coefficients composed with
  the inverse of the glyph's affine), a white fill at the subtree opacity,
  PAINT_POP.
- `engine/core/src/lib.rs`, `engine/wasm/src/lib.rs`: `ui_glyph_misses` and
  `ui_glyph_missed(i)`, the distinct missed codepoints, ascending.
- `framework/compiler/bake-font.ts`: `bakeVectorSlot`, the atlas's metric
  formulas in wider fields; `bakeAtlases` bakes a slot as one when the
  literal says `text-vector` or the atlas cell would pass 255 px, where 0002
  refused. A face carrying COLR draws its glyphs as layers: in a vector slot
  as the glyph, in an atlas slot as an empty cell that widens nothing plus a
  supplement. A colour glyph the core cannot draw, and a codepoint that is a
  picture only inside a shaped sequence (regional indicators, ZWJ, skin-tone
  modifiers, the keycap, tags), are left out of the slot and listed by the
  build, so the text misses and is reported.
- `framework/compiler/colr.ts`: COLR v0 and v1 and CPAL palette 0, the v1
  paint graph flattened to layers. Refused by name: sweep gradients, radial
  gradients whose circles do not share a centre, colour lines that repeat or
  reflect or hold more than six stops, composites, variable paints, a glyph
  clipped by another, the text colour inside a gradient. Angles through
  `cosSinDeg`, never `Math.sin`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `text-vector`, which must sit beside a
  text size in its literal; a vector slot is dynamic and never shares a slot
  with the atlas of its size. `text-[N]` takes up to 4096 px (was 512).
- `tools/build.ts`: `--font-fallback=<path>`, repeatable, tried after
  `fonts.json`'s list; a line per vector slot saying why it is one, per slot
  with colour glyphs, and per reason a codepoint was left out; the
  supplements written into the pak.

In this repository the sidecar's `fonts.fallback` is the flag's only source
(`src/cli/resolve.ts`), `check` fails on a missed codepoint naming the text
nodes that carry it, `trace` and `render` print it, `render --spec` refuses
the job (`src/text/missing.ts`).

Red cases, each watched by `baselines/vector-glyphs/redcheck.ts`, are listed
in `baselines/vector-glyphs.md`.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

